    "body": "## Summary\n- reject previously submitted proposals once the proposer account is suspended\n- apply the guard to both acceptance funding preview and final acceptance\n- ensure rejection happens before escrow reads/mutations, wallet reads, assignment, persistence, or block checks\n- add focused regression tests for both financial paths\n\n## Risk addressed\nAccount suspension currently cancels the suspended user's own open jobs, but their previously submitted proposals on other users' open jobs remain `SUBMITTED`. Without this guard an owner can still preview funding and accept such a proposal, causing escrow adjustment and assignment to a suspended worker.\n\n## Validation\nGitHub Actions must pass on the exact PR head before merge. Merge only with a merge commit after confirming `master` has not moved (or safely updating the branch if it has).",
